## 📌 Overview & Business Problem

E-commerce platforms accumulate **millions of unstructured text reviews**, making manual sentiment auditing impossible at scale. This project builds an automated **Natural Language Processing (NLP) pipeline** on the **Amazon Fine Food Reviews dataset** (500K+ reviews) to classify customer sentiment into **Negative, Neutral, and Positive** categories.

**Business Value:**
- 🎯 Enables product teams to instantly surface customer pain points at scale
- 📉 Detects early warning signs of product quality issues via negative sentiment spikes
- 🔍 Powers automated review moderation and customer feedback triage systems
- 📊 Provides a benchmarked, tunable ML baseline for production-grade sentiment classifiers

---

## ✨ Key Features

- 🧹 **Automated Text Preprocessing Pipeline** — HTML/URL stripping, negation-aware stopword filtering, regex tokenization, and Porter Stemming
- ⚖️ **Stratified Sampling & Class Mapping** — 5-star ratings intelligently mapped to a 3-class sentiment schema (Negative / Neutral / Positive)
- ☁️ **Sentiment-Specific Word Clouds** — Custom HSL color-coded visualizations per sentiment class with generic-word filtering
- 🔢 **TF-IDF Vectorization** — Unigram + Bigram features with sublinear term-frequency scaling (100K max features)
- 🤖 **Dual Model Benchmarking** — `Multinomial Naive Bayes` vs. `Logistic Regression` (class-balanced)
- 🎛️ **Hyperparameter Tuning** — `GridSearchCV` with 3-fold cross-validation optimizing macro F1-score
- 📈 **Comprehensive Evaluation Suite** — Accuracy, Precision, Recall, macro/weighted F1, and full classification reports

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack & Architecture

| Layer                  | Technology                                         |
|-------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------|
| **Language**            | Python 3.10+                                        |
| **Data Handling**       | Pandas, NumPy                                        |
| **NLP Processing**      | NLTK (Stopwords, Porter Stemmer, Regexp Tokenizer)   |
| **Feature Engineering** | scikit-learn `TfidfVectorizer`                       |
| **Modeling**            | `MultinomialNB`, `LogisticRegression`, `GridSearchCV`|
| **Visualization**       | Matplotlib, Seaborn, WordCloud                       |
| **Environment**         | Jupyter Notebook / Google Colab                      |

